{"id": "fef2266b-6a99-40ba-83ab-b31a5e2d0811", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T18:43:03.568898", "source": "user", "parent_id": "4586391b-e39e-4582-adcf-50f0786d03d2", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Initial inspection request. Please report on the following and produce nothing else in this turn except for these items plus any items you mark as strictly necessary for an initial plan; do NOT draft the full experiment design yet. This is a design-only task — execution is not required and must not be simulated as if it were done. Items requested, all source-grounded where possible: 1) Repository / input inspection. List the contents of /workspace (top-level tree, plus one level deeper for any code, docs, configs, or datasets you actually find). For each item, note whether it appears to be code, documentation, configuration, or data. If a files_manifest.txt, README, track.md, or dataset card exists, quote the lines that describe how the DrivAerNet++ parametric inputs and the drag target are organized (number of samples per body style, train/val/test splits if any, feature column names, target units). If no DrivAerNet++ files are present, say so explicitly and do not invent counts. 2) Available compute and toolkit. Confirm whether Python 3, NumPy, pandas, scikit-learn, PyTorch/TensorFlow, XGBoost, and matplotlib are present (use `python3 -c 'import …'` or a quick version check). Note the absence of a GUI/network and that the bubblewrap environment has no GPU. 3) Proposed approach (outline only, not the full design). Sketch the candidate experimental design answering: does predictive performance of parametric-data surrogate models improve with training-set size, and does it differ across model architectures for aerodynamic drag (Cd or Cd·A — confirm which target DrivAerNet++ provides, do not assume). List candidate models to compare (e.g., linear/Ridge baseline, Random Forest, Gradient Boosting/XGBoost, Gaussian Process, MLP), the training-set sizes to sweep, the evaluation metric, the cross-validation / split strategy (and whether body-style stratification is needed), and the repeated-seed protocol. Describe how you will visualize scaling (e.g., test error vs. N curves per model) and test for architecture differences. 4) Assumptions and uncertainties. Enumerate every setup choice that is not pinned down by the supplied documents and that you would need to assume, including: target variable definition, unit, allowable data leakage controls, distribution of body styles across sweeps, hyperparameter budget per model, error-bar procedure, and statistical test for architecture-difference. Flag which assumptions are reversible after the researcher provides information and which are fixed by what track.md / DrivAerNet++ docs state. Stop after these four items; wait for the approach review before producing the final design document.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"Does the predictive performance of surrogate models based on parametric data improve with increased training set size and differ across model architectures in aerodynamic drag prediction? This experiment uses aerodynamic car designs characterized by 26 parameters—as provided in the DrivAerNet++ dataset, which includes diverse configurations such as fastback, notchback, and estateback—for assessing performance scalability and model-specific behavior.\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 24, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 1}
