{"id": "35eae56d-d34a-41da-80f8-ee8e3a8767c8", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T18:47:07.283177", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "2abcd365-d794-43ff-93f0-bcf030ccb638", "action": {"command": "cat >> /workspace/experiment_design.md <<'MARKDOWN'\n\n---\n\n## 9. Feasibility in the Bubblewrap CPU-Only Environment\n\n### 9.1 Environment snapshot (as inspected, see §11)\n- CPU: 24 cores. GPU: **none** (`nvidia-smi` cannot communicate with the driver).\n- Python 3.12.3 available.\n- Network: **disabled** (`curl https://pypi.org` fails DNS).\n- No ML/data libraries preinstalled (numpy, pandas, scipy, scikit-learn, torch, xgboost, matplotlib, seaborn, joblib, optuna, gpytorch, tensorflow all import-fail).\n- GUI: none.\n\n### 9.2 Dependencies needed before any execution (offline install required)\nIn order of criticality:\n1. **`numpy`** — required by everything else (and by the §9.4 NP-only fallbacks).\n2. **`pandas`** — preferred for §2.4 schema validation; `numpy.genfromtxt` is the fallback.\n3. **`scikit-learn`** — required for Models 1–4 and the preferred MLP; also provides `RandomizedSearchCV` for the §5.5 equalized budget.\n4. **`scipy`** — required for Wilcoxon, Friedman, NLPD, Holm–Bonferroni.\n5. **`xgboost`** — preferred for Model 3; sklearn GradientBoosting / HistGradientBoosting are the fallbacks.\n6. **`matplotlib`** — required for §8.1 figures.\n7. **`joblib`** — recommended for sklearn parallelism; not strictly required.\n\nAll of these must be **offline-installed** (wheels pre-staged in the bubblewrap) because `pip` cannot reach an index.\n\n### 9.3 GPU-dependent arms\n**None.** This design is CPU-only by construction. Model 5 (MLP) is sized to fit comfortably on 24 CPU threads. Model 4 (GP) is the training-cost bottleneck but is not a GPU problem.\n\n### 9.4 Wall-clock budget per (model, N) cell\nPer-cell cap = 1500 s of hyperparameter selection (25 trials × 60 s) + a final re-fit on `outer_train ∪ outer_val` + scoring on `outer_test`. Indicative orders of magnitude (CPU, not measured):\n\n| Model | N = 50 | N = 200 | N = 800 | N = 1600 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Ridge | << 60 s | << 60 s | << 60 s | << 60 s |\n| Random Forest (≤ 500 trees) | ≤ 60 s | ≤ 300 s | ≤ 800 s | ≤ 1500 s |\n| XGBoost / GradientBoosting | ≤ 60 s | ≤ 200 s | ≤ 600 s | ≤ 1200 s |\n| GP (exact, Matérn) | ≤ 60 s | ≤ 600 s | ~ 30 min (cap-bound) | not run → GP-sub fallback |\n| MLP (sklearn, ≤ 200 epochs, ≤ 128 hidden) | ≤ 60 s | ≤ 200 s | ≤ 800 s | ≤ 1500 s |\n\nThe total wall-clock consumption across the experiment is bounded by: `|N_grid| × 5 models × K×S replicates × per-fit cost + selection cap`. Without measured `N_total` (no dataset present) the exact total cannot be quoted, but the per-cell cap of 1500 s makes a worst-case upper bound of `6 × 5 × 25 × 1500 s = 1,125,000 s ≈ 13 days` of sequential computation if every cell runs to cap. In practice most cells finish well under cap and parallelism across the 24 cores can drag this down by roughly the number of cells run in parallel.\n\n### 9.5 Largest N at which exact GP is feasible\n**N = 2000**, set in §6. The cap is set by the cubic cost (`O(N³)` for exact GP) plus the 1500 s per-cell hyperparameter budget, not by a numerical inversion issue. Above N = 2000 the GP arm switches to the `GP-sub` fallback (randomly drawn 2000-row subset, drawn once per replicate and logged).\n\nMARKDOWN\necho \"section 9 appended\"\nwc -l /workspace/experiment_design.md", "timeout_seconds": 60, "kind": "ExecuteCheckAction"}, "tool_name": "execute_check", "tool_call_id": "call-4688d4dd-8f47-4e45-9597-f4dcaab1a2aa", "tool_call": {"id": "call-4688d4dd-8f47-4e45-9597-f4dcaab1a2aa", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "execute_check", "arguments": "{\"summary\": \"Append section 9 to experiment_design.md\", \"command\": \"cat >> /workspace/experiment_design.md <<'MARKDOWN'\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Feasibility in the Bubblewrap CPU-Only Environment\\n\\n### 9.1 Environment snapshot (as inspected, see \\u00a711)\\n- CPU: 24 cores. GPU: **none** (`nvidia-smi` cannot communicate with the driver).\\n- Python 3.12.3 available.\\n- Network: **disabled** (`curl https://pypi.org` fails DNS).\\n- No ML/data libraries preinstalled (numpy, pandas, scipy, scikit-learn, torch, xgboost, matplotlib, seaborn, joblib, optuna, gpytorch, tensorflow all import-fail).\\n- GUI: none.\\n\\n### 9.2 Dependencies needed before any execution (offline install required)\\nIn order of criticality:\\n1. **`numpy`** \\u2014 required by everything else (and by the \\u00a79.4 NP-only fallbacks).\\n2. **`pandas`** \\u2014 preferred for \\u00a72.4 schema validation; `numpy.genfromtxt` is the fallback.\\n3. **`scikit-learn`** \\u2014 required for Models 1\\u20134 and the preferred MLP; also provides `RandomizedSearchCV` for the \\u00a75.5 equalized budget.\\n4. **`scipy`** \\u2014 required for Wilcoxon, Friedman, NLPD, Holm\\u2013Bonferroni.\\n5. **`xgboost`** \\u2014 preferred for Model 3; sklearn GradientBoosting / HistGradientBoosting are the fallbacks.\\n6. **`matplotlib`** \\u2014 required for \\u00a78.1 figures.\\n7. **`joblib`** \\u2014 recommended for sklearn parallelism; not strictly required.\\n\\nAll of these must be **offline-installed** (wheels pre-staged in the bubblewrap) because `pip` cannot reach an index.\\n\\n### 9.3 GPU-dependent arms\\n**None.** This design is CPU-only by construction. Model 5 (MLP) is sized to fit comfortably on 24 CPU threads. Model 4 (GP) is the training-cost bottleneck but is not a GPU problem.\\n\\n### 9.4 Wall-clock budget per (model, N) cell\\nPer-cell cap = 1500 s of hyperparameter selection (25 trials \\u00d7 60 s) + a final re-fit on `outer_train \\u222a outer_val` + scoring on `outer_test`. Indicative orders of magnitude (CPU, not measured):\\n\\n| Model | N = 50 | N = 200 | N = 800 | N = 1600 |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Ridge | << 60 s | << 60 s | << 60 s | << 60 s |\\n| Random Forest (\\u2264 500 trees) | \\u2264 60 s | \\u2264 300 s | \\u2264 800 s | \\u2264 1500 s |\\n| X